    "code_released": "https://github.com/ege-erdogan/equivariant-sae",
    "peer_reviewed": "preprint",
    "problems": "The paper’s toy experiment imposes the feature structure rather than demonstrating that a trained network naturally develops it. Feature recovery and detection are proxies, not direct measurements of overlap, angles, interference, or feature importance. Main toy-plot values are not numerically stated; the numerical appendix table reports random canonical representatives and standard deviations.",
    "rows_left_out": "No additional rows left out under the 60-row limit. Reconstruction results are not included because reconstruction error does not measure the listed claim versions. Results on shape, galaxy, and blood-cell model probing are not included because they concern downstream usefulness of SAE representations rather than the specified superposition, polysemanticity, or LLM feature claims.",
